<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Portal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Portal is a city in western Uganda at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwenzori-mountains">Rwenzori Mountains</a>. It grew around a British fort of 1893 named after the diplomat Sir Gerald Portal, and became the capital of the Toro kingdom, with the royal palace on a hill above the town. It is a centre of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a>-growing region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-portal.jpg" alt="Fort Portal" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dave Proffer · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Portal_-_Flickr_-_Dave_Proffer_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
